{
  "about": "Odia glossary for drharshmaheshwari.com. Every Odia translation must use these terms: tests/i18n.test.mjs checks that when an English text contains a term, its Odia has one of the accepted forms. Change a term here, then retranslate what uses it. docs/translation.md has the rules. Spelling: ୟ (U+0B5F) for ya-phala sounds as in modern print, ଡ଼ for the flapped da.",
  "register": "Everyday spoken Odia that a family in Bhubaneswar or Cuttack would use, not heavily Sanskritised. Common English health words that people say in Odia stay as they are said (BMI, ବ୍ଲଡ ସୁଗାର, ଡାଇବେଟିସ୍, ବ୍ଲଡ ପ୍ରେସର). Polite 'ଆପଣ'. Short sentences ending in '।'. Numbers in 0-9, never Odia digits. Units as in English (cm, kg).",
